Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/aroma-affymetrix/c/3gDyHrKELdw/m/07UnnSToxroJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Late but note too late.  Note:

units <- indexOf(cdf, names="2315554")

is *not* the same as:

units <- indexOf(cdf, "2315554")

The latter is instead the same as:

units <- indexOf(cdf, pattern="2315554")

The first one using 'names' will return units with the specified names
(you can specify a vector of names), whereas the one with 'pattern'
will return units with names matching the regular expression "2315554"
(you can only specify a single regular expression string).

Thus:

units <- indexOf(cdf, pattern="^2315554$")

would return the same as:

units <- indexOf(cdf, names="2315554")

Hope this clarifies what is going on.

/Henrik

